      "source": "Wu Blockchain (Telegram)",
      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "SafePal Users Targeted by Physical Mail Phishing Following Data Breach According to Italian crypto media outlet Criptovaluta it, hardware wallet maker SafePal’s data breach has led to physical mail phishing attacks targeting Italian users. Fraudulent letters impersonating SafePal claim that recipients’ hardware wallets have a firmware security vulnerability and contain QR codes that direct users via Arweave to a fake SafePal website. Both the letters and the phishing website contain accurate customer names, addresses and order details. Between March 2025 and April 2026, an issue with an order-tracking plugin exposed the personal data of nearly 40,000 SafePal customers, including names, email addresses and mailing addresses. SafePal previously confirmed that attackers had been using the leaked data for phishing attempts. — link",
